    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/XMLNAME-2025---2026-FWS-Student-Worker--Team-Manager_R2965": {
      "title": "2026-2027 FWS Student Worker, Team Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-14\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary Student Managers play a vital role in the daily operations of Saint Leo University Athletics. The purpose of the Team Manager Program is to provide support to the Department of Athletics and its varsity programs in all areas of team operations. Team managers are assigned to work with a specific team and assist the coaching staff during practices and competitions. Responsibilities may also include support with equipment, recruiting logistics, and travel coordination. Job Description Please note: Hiring for this position is subject to funding availability and a limited number of openings. Applying does not guarantee employment. Benefits of being a team manager: Opportunities for leadership and professional networking Hands-on experience in collegiate athletics alongside coaches, student-athletes, support staff, and administrators Develop lasting relationships within the athletic community Potential opportunities to travel to away competitions (select positions) Team managers are needed across multiple varsity programs within the department. If you're interested in gaining valuable experience in a collegiate athletics environment, this is a great opportunity to get involved and contribute to the success of our teams. Note:  If you are wanting to work for a specific team, please make a note of it on your cover letter. Duties and Tasks: Practice & game day setup and breakdown Laundry duties for items such as practice and game uniforms Observe or perform administrative duties during practice & games (track stats, run clock, filming, etc.) Assist with community service and fundraising events Other duties as assigned by coaching staff or athletic department staff member REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Must follow all University, NCAA, and team rules Knowledge of sport is preferred but not required Must be able to work evening and weekends Hours will vary during in season/out of season Ability to work in various weather elements such as heat, cold, & rain Required Skills: Reliability, Dependability, Punctuality, Self-Confidence EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS / QUALIFICATIONS: Federal Work Study required Must be a current or incoming full-time student (minimum 12 credit hours per semester) Must be in good academic standing Previous team manager experience, sport knowledge, and/or training/playing is preferred but not required Physical Demands:   Some lifting may be required Working with an outdoor team may involve extended exposure to varying weather conditions, including heat or cold. Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
    },
    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/XMLNAME-2026-2027-FWS-Student-Worker--Dining-Services_R2870": {
      "title": "2026-2027 FWS Student Worker, Benedicts Coffeehouse",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-10\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary Applicants for this position will be assigned Food Services related tasks at Benedicts Coffeehouse. Tasks will encompass all aspects of food service operation from food prep, to food services, to cleaning & stocking. Job Description Please note: Hiring for this position is subject to funding availability and a limited number of openings. Applying does not guarantee employment. Responsibilities: Clean service stations and equipment. Prepare a variety of foods according to customers' orders or supervisors’ instructions while following approved procedures. Follow all HAACP rules and regulations. Ability to interact with staff members, students, parents, and others in an open, friendly business-like manner. Break down food items at the end of each day's meal periods and properly store them (covers, labels, and stores all food items). Performs other tasks as assigned and/or required.   Qualifications: Must be awarded Work Study as part of Financial Aid award. Previous Foodservice/Retail Experience preferred but not required. ENVIRONMENT: The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office, the University, and at various off campus sites including overnight travel, handle various type of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe, and assess. The employee is occas