    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/XMLNAME-2026-2027-NFWS-Student-Worker--Accessibility-Peer-Mentor_R2263": {
      "title": "2026-2027 NFWS Student Worker, Accessibility Peer Mentor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-09\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The Accessibility Peer Mentor supports Saint Leo University’s mission of assisting students with disabilities as they navigate academic and campus life. Acting as a peer role model, the mentor promotes independence, confidence, and engagement through informal guidance, companionship, and help accessing campus resources. Mentors do not perform instructional duties, complete academic work on behalf of students, or serve in a clinical or counseling capacity. The role is designed to create natural, student-led engagement that fosters belonging and self-advocacy. Job Description Please note: Hiring for this position is subject to funding availability and a limited number of openings. Applying does not guarantee employment. Primary Responsibilities:   Attend regularly scheduled events, classes, meals, and study sessions with assigned mentee(s)   Serve as a study partner and peer resource, helping mentees remain on task and build academic routines   Support mentees in accessing campus services, including tutoring, advising, wellness, and extracurricular programs   Attend at least   two   university-sponsored on-campus events with mentee(s) each semester   Participate in pre-semester training prior to standard student move-in   Attend ongoing training and weekly staff meetings throughout the academic year   Provide general support to Accessibility Services and broader Student Affairs Division functions as assigned   Model behavior consistent with the University's Core Values   Qualifications:   Required:   Full-time enrollment in a Saint Leo University undergraduate or graduate program   Good academic and judicial standing throughout employment   Demonstrated ability to work independently and uphold professional boundaries   Commitment to inclusivity and support for students with diverse needs, including autism spectrum disorder and/or developmental disabilities   Consistent demonstration of Saint Leo’s Core Values   Preferred:   Background or coursework in education, psychology, social work, or related human services fields   Prior experience in peer support roles (e.g., tutor, RA, orientation leader)   Involvement in university clubs, organizations, or student leadership   Familiarity with ADA principles and disability-inclusive practices   Work Environment:   This role takes place on campus and may include walking long distances, navigating crowded spaces, and participating in various campus settings. Mentors are expected to:   Communicate professionally in person, by phone, and electronically   Move frequently throughout campus   Use various tools and equipment for academic or social engagement   Occasionally lift up to 10 pounds   Reasonable accommodations will be provided in accordance with the ADA to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform essential job functions.   Notice:   This job description outlines representative responsibilities and qualifications for the Accessibility Mentor role. It is not exhaustive and may be adjusted based on departmental needs. Additional related duties may be assigned as appropriate .   Saint Leo University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity as critical to the success of our students, faculty, and staff.     Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
    },
    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/XMLNAME-2026--2027-FWS-Student-Worker--Accessibility-Services-Student-Assistant_R2230": {
      "title": "2026-2027 FWS Student Worker, Accessibility Services Student Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-09\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The Accessibility Services Assistant plays a vital role in supporting the office’s mission to ensure all students have equitable access to education. This position involves assisting with daily office operations, digital accessibility work, and student-facing support. All work must be approached with care, empathy, and professionalism, in alignment with Saint Leo University’s Core Values. Job Description Please note: Hiring for this position is subject to funding availability and a limited number of openings. Applying does not guarantee employment. General Responsibilities   Answer phones, take messages, and forward calls to professional staff as directed .   Greet and assist all office visitors; help maintain an organized, confidential workspace.   Help students navigate the AIM platform and campus support resources.   Perform clerical tasks including scanning, organizing files, and basic data entry.   Participate in required training sessions and weekly team meetings.   Provide professional and courteous customer service.   Support other Student Affairs units as assigned by supervisor.   Accessibility Services-Specific Responsibilities   Convert textbooks and course materials into alternative digital formats as directed.   Maintain accurate student records within the AIM platform.   Provide peer support under supervision (e.g., guidance with assistive tech logins, printing).   Use specialized software (e.g., screen readers, text-to-speech tools) to test functionality.   Assist in maintaining a lending library of devices and accessibility tools.   Help develop visual guides or short tutorials for students using assistive technology.   Participate in departmental outreach efforts by calling or emailing students with reminders or check-ins.   Assist with event logistics including tabling, setup, and student check-ins.   Co-create digital content and social media posts about available accommodations, tips, and resources using tools such as Canva.   Qualifications   Required:   Must be Federal Work Study eligible and approved.   Demonstrated patience and maturity in handling sensitive information.   Attention to detail and ability to follow technical instructions.   Basic computer skills including file formatting and web navigation.   Demonstrate professionalism and commitment to the Saint Leo University Core Values.   Ability to treat all individuals with dignity and respect, especially in sensitive or confidential contexts.   Preferred:   Familiarity with assistive technology platforms (e.g., Kurzweil, Read&Write , JAWS).   Comfort with calling and emailing students in a professional manner.   Interest in education, psychology, health sciences, or technology.   Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
