    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/Campus-Safety-Officer_R6655": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Campus Safety Officer is a uniformed, unarmed, Florida Class “D” licensed security professional who protects the life, safety, and property of Saint Leo University students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Officers provide visible patrol, access control, event support, and first response to medical, fire, and safety incidents, 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. Officers serve as approachable, community-oriented representatives of the University and carry out their duties consistent with Saint Leo’s Catholic Benedictine values of community, respect, and hospitality. Officers are not sworn law enforcement officers. They hold no greater legal authority than a private citizen and coordinate with the Pasco County Sheriff’s Office (PCSO), which has primary law enforcement jurisdiction over the campus, for any incident that exceeds that authority. Job Description Patrol and Access Control   Conduct foot, golf cart, and marked-vehicle patrol of assigned zones, including building and lock checks, residence hall access-control procedures, and documented checks of the Saint Leo Academy residential area.  Provide escort services, parking and traffic direction, and welfare checks, including missing-student protocols.  Verify identification of unfamiliar persons, and issue University trespass warnings in coordination with PCSO.  Emergency and Incident Response   Respond first to fire alarms, intrusion alarms, and medical emergencies; provide first aid, CPR, and AED care within training and certification until Fire Rescue, EMS, or PCSO arrives.  Respond to fights, alcohol- and substance-related incidents, and mental health crises using verbal de-escalation first, and summon PCSO whenever a weapon, felony, serious injury, or situation beyond private-person authority is involved.  Support active-threat, lockdown, bomb-threat, and severe weather procedures, following PCSO direction and the University’s emergency notification protocols.  Provide a clear verbal handoff to responding PCSO deputies and preserve the scene.  Use of Force and Legal Compliance   Use only the minimum objectively reasonable force, as defined by the University’s Use of Force Policy and Florida law, and de-escalate at the earliest safe opportunity. Officers never carry firearms and never use or threaten deadly force.  Carry and use OC spray and restraints only while current in certification, and disengage and summon PCSO when a situation cannot be safely resolved.  Event Support   Staff athletic contests, commencement, orientation, move-in/move-out, concerts, and other campus events, maintaining a visible, approachable presence and assisting with crowd flow, access points, and rapid response.  Minors and Special Populations   Follow heightened-duty-of-care procedures for Saint Leo Academy students, who are minors, including de-escalation as the required first response and release of minors only to authorized persons.  Report suspected abuse or neglect of any minor immediately to the Florida Abuse Hotline as a mandatory reporter, in parallel with internal notification.  Documentation, Equipment, and Training   Write accurate, timely incident, use-of-force, trespass, alarm, and shift reports; submit a Use of Force Report before the end of shift for any force at Level 4 (mechanical restraint) or above.  Inspect the duty belt, patrol vehicle, and golf cart at the start of every shift, restock used supplies, and tag deficient equipment out of service.  Complete the 80-hour Field Training Officer program before solo patrol and a minimum of 40 hours of in-service training every calendar year.  Wear the issued uniform and University ID visibly while on duty and meet grooming standards. Perform other duties as assigned.  AUTHORITY AND LIMITATIONS   Campus Safety Officers operate as a licensed private security function under Chapter 493, Florida Statutes. Officers may detain a person they directly witness committing a felony or breach of the peace, using reasonable non-deadly force, for the sole purpose of holding the person until PCSO arrives. Officers may not make formal arrests, conduct searches or seizures beyond those available to any private citizen, or pursue fleeing persons into traffic or unreasonable danger.  REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS   Current, unrestricted Florida Class “D” Security Officer License (FDACS), verified before an offer of employment and maintained through each two-year renewal.  Satisfactory criminal history background check, reference verification, and University suitability screening.  Ability to obtain and maintain CPR/AED/First Aid, OC spray, and restraint certifications during training; no Officer may work a solo post with an expired certification.  Valid driver’s license and the ability to be certified to operate the patrol vehicle and golf carts.   High school diploma or equivalent.   Ability to communicate clearly by radio and in writing, write clear reports, and remain calm and courteous under pressure.  Willingness to work 12-hour day or night shifts on a rotating squad schedule, including weekends, holidays, special events, and inclement-weather activations.  For Officers assigned to the Saint Leo Academy residential area: Level 2 background screening under Chapter 435 and Section 1012.32, Florida Statutes.  Preferred   Experience in security, law enforcement, military, or campus safety, particularly in a residential college or school setting.  Training in de-escalation, mental health crisis intervention, or Clery Act and Title IX reporting.  Commitment to serving a diverse student population, including international and first-generation students, in keeping with the University’s Benedictine values. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORK ENVIRONMENT   Work is performed outdoors and indoors in all weather and at all hours. The role requires extended periods of standing, walking, and driving; the ability to respond quickly on foot; the physical ability to perform first aid and CPR; and the ability to apply defensive and control techniques as trained. Officers must be able to wear the standard uniform and duty belt for an entire 12-hour shift. Reasonable accommodations will be made for qualified individuals with disabilities in accordance with applicable law.  ENVIRONMENT:   The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office and University, handle various type of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess.   The employee is occasionally required to lift up to 10 pounds unless otherwise specified in the job description. NOTICE: The intent of this job description is to provide a representation of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and shall not be construed as a declaration of the total specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position.  Employees may be directed to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description.  Saint Leo University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity as a critical step in ensuring employee, student and graduate success.  Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
    },
    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/XMLNAME-2027-Spring-Orientation-Leader_R6587": {
      "title": "2027 Spring Orientation Leader",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The position of Orientation Leader (OL) is one that allows a student to make a substantial contribution to Saint Leo University and a lasting first impression on incoming students. OLs help new students and their families in making a positive transition to Saint Leo University. Ols are extremely knowledgeable about campus resources and student success strategies. OLs must understand and support the goals and objectives of the New Student Orientation (NSO) program. Below are the basic OL job responsibilities: 1. University Representative 2. Team Member/Leader 3. Facilitator 4. Event Execution An OL is required to be on campus 1.5 to 2 weeks prior to the start of the upcoming semester for training and planning. ***In addition to uploading resume, the following documents are required for consideration. *** 1. Cover Letter 2. References (minimum of 2) Job Description REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: Responsibilities: To serve as a positive role model and resource for new students and their families To initiate and develop an open communication with faculty, advisors, staff, students, and family members attending NSO To work with faculty and staff members, other OLs, and members of Saint Leo administration to facilitate the success of all aspects of the NSO program. To lead tours and discussion groups for incoming students and/or parents To serve as a representative of Saint Leo in a variety of situations including social functions and meals To assist in preparation, implementation and evaluation of NSO To perform other duties as deemed necessary by the Student Success professional staff To actively participate in training to become knowledgeable on various aspects of the University Mentor relationships with new students   QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum 2.5 cumulative GPA Current full-time student Good judicial standing A passion for helping others Ability to work independently as well as with a team, and a willingness to both lead and follow Interpersonal communication skills Reliability, creativity, stamina, flexibility/adaptability, and punctuality Ability to relate to and work with a variety of personality types and diverse groups of people (students, parents, faculty, both professional and student staff) A positive attitude and a sense of humor Ability to work under limited supervision Ability to work long hours (10-15hrs and/or early or late shifts) Able to handle constructive criticism Familiarity with Saint Leo programs and services   ENVIRONMENT:     The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position.   While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office and University, handle various types of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess. The employee is occasionally required to lift up to 10 pounds unless otherwise specified in the job description.   NOTICE: This job description intends to provide a representation of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and shall not be construed as a declaration of the total specific duties and responsibilities of any position. Employees may be directed to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description.  Saint Leo University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity as a critical step in ensuring employee, student, and graduate success.    Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
    },
    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/Graduate-Assistant---Men-s-Tennis_R6548": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Men's Tennis",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary Under the supervision and guidance of a head coach, the graduate assistant (GA) coach aids in all phases of coaching and mentorship of the Division II Men’s Tennis program including student-athlete recruitment, game preparation, player evaluation, academic coordination and practice and game day coaching. Job Description Duties and Tasks: Assists head coach in teaching team members the individual skills and techniques associated with the sport. Assists head coach in implementing game tactics and strategy.  Guides team members on proper nutrition needed for optimal performance at the collegiate level.  Guides team members through strength and conditioning training. Mentors team members on proper time management strategies to balance academic and athletic team demands. Mentors team captain on leadership.  To instruct, monitor, counsel and assist student athletes to make sure that they meet satisfactory progress and eligibility rules. Provides appropriate leadership, direction, and supervision relevant to the academic progress and personal development of student-athletes within the program Create a positive and productive environment for the student-athletes. Assists with scheduling opponents with a proportional amount of home and away, conference and non-conference and regional games. Assists with monitoring academic success for student athletes To be knowledgeable and follow all University, Conference and NCAA rules and regulations. Adherence to NCAA Division II, SSC, and Saint Leo University rules and regulations, supporting the philosophy, goals, and mission of the University and its intercollegiate athletics program as well as adherence to departmental policies and procedures. Perform other coaching related duties as assigned.   REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:   Knowledge: Knowledge of coaching tennis tactics and techniques Bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited college/university NCAA rules and compliance Skills: Leadership skills Well-developed interpersonal communication skills to deal with recruits and their parents Valid Driver’s License Abilities: Ability to motivate student-athletes Ability to effectively work with collegiate student-athletes Ability to recruit student athletes Demonstrated ability to use computer programs Ability to demonstrate proper tennis techniques, set-up and move equipment needed for practice and games   ENVIRONMENT:     The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position.   While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office and University, handle various type of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess.   The employee is occasionally required to lift up to 10 pounds unless otherwise specified in the job description.   NOTICE: The intent of this job description is to provide a representation of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and shall not be construed as a declaration of the total specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position.  Employees may be directed to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description.  Saint Leo University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity as a critical step in ensuring employee, student and graduate success.  Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
